{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And these are the sons of Dishan.</b> This is Dishon mentioned above at the beginning of the section, the fifth son of Seir. Scripture calls him sometimes דישון, sometimes דישן, for they are one and the same, like חירום and חירם — as it is written (1 Kings 7:40) ״ויעש חירום את הכיורות״, and it is written (ibid.) ״ויכל חירם״. But when they appear in a single verse, one is called דישון and the other דישן, for they were two chieftains (אלופים), and therefore Scripture designates them with variant forms in order to distinguish between the two."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:01.611643194Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}